@startuml PlayVsAI_UseCaseClassDiagram
title Use Case: Play vs AI (incl. Choose Difficulty) - Participating Classes

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
hide empty members

enum Difficulty {
  EASY
  NORMAL
}


class UIManager <<boundary>> {
  - currentScreen : Screen
  + showScreen(s : Screen) : void
  + renderBoard(b : Board, isOwn : boolean) : void
  + onCellClick(c : Coordinate) : void
}

class Game <<controller>> {
  - currentTurn : Player
  + beginBattle() : void
  + fireShot(shooter : Player, target : Coordinate) : Shot
  + switchTurn() : void
  + checkWinCondition() : boolean
}

abstract class Player <<entity>> {
  - name : String
  + {abstract} chooseTarget() : Coordinate
}

class HumanPlayer <<entity>> {
  + chooseTarget() : Coordinate
}

class AIOpponent <<entity>> {
  - difficulty : Difficulty
  - huntQueue : List<Coordinate>
  + chooseTarget() : Coordinate
  + shouldUseAbility() : boolean
  - hunt() : Coordinate
  - target() : Coordinate
}

class Board <<entity>> {
  + placeFleetRandomly() : void
  + receiveShot(target : Coordinate) : Shot
  + hasBeenTargeted(c : Coordinate) : boolean
}

class Shot <<entity>> {
  - result : ShotResult
  + isHit() : boolean
}

' ---------- Relationships ----------
UIManager ..> Game : calls directly >
Game "1" o-- "2" Player : players >
Game "1" *-- "0..*" Shot : history >
Player <|-- HumanPlayer
Player <|-- AIOpponent
Player "1" *-- "1" Board : owns >
AIOpponent --> Difficulty
AIOpponent ..> Board : reads opponent's shots >
AIOpponent ..> Shot : remembers hits >

note bottom of Game
  Client-only: Server and NetworkHandler
  are not involved. The same Game, Board
  and Ship classes run in the browser, so
  the rules are identical to multiplayer.
end note

note right of AIOpponent
  NORMAL: hunt on a checkerboard
  (row + col even), then target the
  4 neighbours of an unsunk hit.
  EASY: random untargeted cell.
end note

@enduml
